<title>USA: WinsLoew to sell Lyon-Shaw unit.</title>
<headline>WinsLoew to sell Lyon-Shaw unit.</headline>
<dateline>PELHAM, Ala. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>WinsLoew Furniture Inc said Monday it had signed a definitive agreement to sell its Lyon-Shaw wrought iron casual furniture unit to Woodard Inc, an affiliate of CC Industries Inc of Chicago.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>WinsLoew said it expects the deal to close August 31.</p>
<p>In 1996 Lyon-Shaw, located in Salisbury, N.C., sold about $11 million of wrought iron casual furniture.</p>
<p>WinsLoew said the sale is part of its ongoing plan to enhance profitability by reducing embedded costs and disposing of non-strategic assets.</p>
</text>
